Resolver patch series on upstream Portage commit bdf046b03 (2026-11-23)
======================================================================

Base: git commit bdf046b03a28a74541c3c31c02244376f85d0790 of proj/portage.git,
fetched as a snapshot tarball. Used by sys-apps/portage-9999-r12::pwr.

  0001-0034   the series of ../ladder-73646c35d/ (its README says what each sub-series
              A-O is, what it needs and what it gives alone), ported patch by patch:
              after each patch every file touched so far was three-way merged (ours =
              73646c35d + patches so far, base = 73646c35d, theirs = bdf046b03). One
              conflict, in every step, in depgraph._select_atoms_probe(): upstream
              80e187989abb gave that probe its own cache (_select_atoms_probe_cache).
              Upstream's function is kept, the series' memo wrapper around it is
              dropped, _select_atoms_probe_imp() of the series is upstream's
              _select_atoms_probe_uncached(), and the helpers of 0029/0031 stand
              before it. All other memos of the series are unchanged.
  0035-0037   sub-series P, stage 5 of the agent runs (2026-11-24). Each of the three
              applies alone, in any subset and in any order (patch -p1 -F0, checked),
              and all three give the same tree whatever the order:
              0035  reuse of whole backtracking attempts across a prune_rebuilds restart
              0036  merge order calculation put off in attempts that restart
              0037  merge order of PDEPEND children independent of the hash seed
                    (a defect of unpatched upstream; no effect on time)
  ../portage-bdf046b03-native-fastpaths.patch              the C modules _hashbase and _cfast
  ../portage-bdf046b03-env-update-below-unmerge-group.patch  env-update no longer hangs
              below a parallel unmerge (both files are the 73646c35d ones: they apply
              with line offsets only)

0001-0034 in numeric order (patch -p1 -F0) give the tree that was measured as "port" on
2026-11-24, byte for byte. Dropping a patch of 0001-0034 follows the rules of the old
README; the port did not make them independent of each other.

Six-state sum of `emerge -p -uND @world` wall seconds, six resolves in parallel, merge
list in order (without the two lines that 0037 fixes) and backtracking attempts equal
to unpatched bdf046b03 in every run. Figures of one row were measured side by side;
the host drifts by several seconds between sessions.

